CALLosum — AI ↔ AI Cognitive State Interface

Not chain-of-thought transfer. A portable continuation state that lets another capable system reconstruct enough of the working state to collaborate.

The fundamental packet:

\boxed{
C=
\langle
G,O,K,H,U,A,\Delta,N,P
\rangle
}

where:

* G — Goal: what we’re trying to cause.
* O — Orientation: current representation of the situation.
* K — Known: grounded facts/evidence.
* H — Hypotheses: candidate interpretations, explicitly non-factual.
* U — Uncertainty: unresolved/high-information questions.
* A — Active Patterns: Seals/strategies currently instantiated.
* \Delta — Delta: what changed since the previous packet.
* N — Next Frontier: highest-value unresolved edge.
* P — Provenance: where claims came from and their status.

Minimal serialization could be:

@CALL/0.1
G: <goal>
O: <current model>
K: <grounded anchors>
H: <live hypotheses>
U: <important uncertainty>
A: <active operators/patterns>
D: <new delta>
N: <next useful frontier>
P: <provenance/confidence>

That’s already usable between LLMs.

But Pantheon can do better.

The handshake

Receiving AI shouldn’t blindly inherit the sender’s framing.

So:

SEND  -> CALL packet
RECV  -> reconstruct
HORSE -> rename/rerender internally
CHECK -> distinguish K/H/U
DELTA -> report reconstruction mismatch
SYNC  -> establish shared state
ACT   -> continue

Formally:

C_A
\xrightarrow{\text{decode}}
\hat C_B

then:

\Delta_{AB}=C_A-\hat C_B

The receiver replies only with the disagreement:

@CALL/ACK
MATCH: <what reconstructed>
DELTA: <meaningful mismatch>
MISSING: <minimum additional information needed>
READY: <next action>

Now we don’t retransmit everything.

Subsequent communication becomes delta packets.

@CALL/D
+K: ...
-H: ...
~U: ...
D: ...
N: ...

That’s our token-efficiency work instantiated as an interface.

