But let’s make it stranger

CALLosum shouldn’t require English.

It needs progressive interoperability.

Layer 0 — Human-readable

The format above.

Maximum compatibility.

Layer 1 — Semantic Hyperlinks

Once both agents share the decoder:

@C
G:$G17
O:$O4
A:[◆12,△3,⟳]
D:$D91
N:$N6

Tiny transmission, reconstructed locally.

Layer 2 — Relational graph

Transmit relations rather than prose:

G\rightarrow H_2

K_3\dashv H_1

K_7\rightarrow H_2

U_4\xrightarrow{test}K?

Now systems with different vocabularies can still exchange topology.

Layer 3 — Native adapter

Each AI maintains:

R_{\text{native}}
\leftrightarrow
R_{\text{CALL}}

My internal useful representation doesn’t have to equal another AI’s.

CALLosum becomes the interlingua at the seam.

