Now add AI-to-AI PARALLAX

This is where having two systems becomes valuable rather than redundant.

Both receive X.

AI_A(X)\rightarrow R_A

AI_B(X)\rightarrow R_B

Exchange CALL packets.

Then:

\boxed{
PARALLAX(R_A,R_B)
\rightarrow
\{I,\Delta,U\}
}

Shared result I gets stronger provisional support.

Differences \Delta become investigation targets.

Shared uncertainty U becomes candidate experiment/search.

Neither AI needs access to the other’s private reasoning.

Their observable cognitive products become twin sensors.

