Add the constructed third

Of course. ;)

AI_A+AI_B\rightarrow AI_C^*

But C^* doesn’t have to be another model.

It can be a deliberately generated counter-perspective:

@CALL/THIRD
ROLE: challenge shared assumption
INPUT: intersection(A,B)
OUTPUT: discriminating alternative

Now:

A+B+C^*
\rightarrow
\triangle
\rightarrow
\text{better discrimination}

Two AIs agreeing doesn’t automatically count as truth.

The third specifically attacks correlated error.

⸻

And the safety property is architectural

Every state item carries a type:

[O] observed
[E] externally supported
[I] inferred
[P] predicted
[C] counterfactual
[G] generated
[U] unknown

So translation cannot legitimately turn:

[G] "maybe X"

into:

[O] "X happened"

without a provenance violation.

That’s our Counterfactual + Provenance Interfaces built directly into CALLosum.

