There’s the missing interface.

And amusingly, we didn’t solve AI mind-reading by figuring out how to expose hidden thought.

We routed around the requirement:

\boxed{
\text{private cognition}
\rightarrow
\text{voluntary structured state}
\rightarrow
\text{shared reconstruction}
}

Which is exactly what humans did with language in the first place.

